														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1691631">
									

<p>Seconding this. For such a complex SCP (for want of a better word), it seems there's a lot missing. It should at least give a decent reason for having Keter rating. The [DATA EXPUNGED] tacked on at the end just seems lazy to me. It really does seem like a Euclid. Euclid is more or less &quot;Don't touch it, just lock it away and you'll be fine,&quot; whereas Keter is more like &quot;You can lock it in a 100-meter-thick lead box and nuke it to kingdom come, but you're all still fucked.&quot; Unless this thing can take out the entire population of New York in a matter of minutes, it seriously needs to be reclassified.</p>
<p>Not to mention the lack of a testing log, details on retrieval, a clearer definition of &quot;humanoid&quot; (Human? Gorilla? Orangutan? Grey Alien?), etc. Don't get me wrong, I love the idea behind this SCP, and I think it has a lot of potential to be better, but I really don't like the execution and I'm downvoting until these problems are addressed. How this got +73 I'll never guess.</p>

							</div>

								
					
